  m_Name: Tutorial_en-US
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en-US
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9696160b5c124cd45ba2823b74450949, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 1282111852544
    m_Localized: Game Tutorial
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1
    m_Localized: 'Welcome to the game <color=green>"Protein Synthesis"</color> Here''s
      a quick tutorial to help you navigate the game without feeling lost.


      If
      you don''t need it, just click the button with the "X" in the <color=green>top
      right corner</color> of this panel.


      To continue the tutorial, simply
      click the arrow to the right in the <color=green>bottom right corner</color>
      of this panel. You can go back to the information until you close this panel,
      so pay close attention.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2
    m_Localized: 'Initially, the most interactive part of the game is at the bottom,
      especially in the <color=green>white bar</color>. It will display the content
      of a <color=green>mission</color>, representing a phase of synthesizing a specific
      protein.


      By clicking on the button with the name of the currently synthesized
      protein, you''ll get more information about the game phases'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3
    m_Localized: If you clicked on the protein button at the bottom (as mentioned
      in the previous session), you noticed that there are some <color=blue>highlighted</color>
      words. If you click on them, an extra page with additional protein information
      will appear.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4
    m_Localized: 'Still talking about the stages on the <color=green>top part</color>,
      there''s a bit of detail about the stage. The content is part of the mission
      text you''ve already seen, but it will always be available.

      

      In
      the <color=green>left box</color>, you''ll find brief information on how to
      play the game in case you forget. They''re short but very useful.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5
    m_Localized: 'A lot of information appears, but it is very diluted, especially
      in the phases, where more information appears, but it is possible to be seen
      again with a <color=green>instructions</color> button if the phase is complex.


      We
      hope you enjoy the game, to start playing just click on the <color=green>close
      button</color> or the <color=green>right arrow in the bottom right corner</color>.


      Have
      fun!!!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6
    m_Localized: Find the cell nucleus to initiate the transcription process and
      carry out the first step of protein synthesis (mission 1)!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7
    m_Localized: Fill in the RNA strand with complementary nucleotides to form the
      messenger RNA molecule. Once formed, direct the molecule out of the nucleus
      through the pores!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8
    m_Localized: Identify the amino acids corresponding to the codons on the mRNA
      strand and enter the correct name of the amino acid in the field below. To
      complete the mission, click "process protein."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9
    m_Localized: In this stage, you'll learn more about the processing of proteins
      after their synthesis in translation. This process is crucial for activating
      and enabling the protein to perform its functions. Click "continue" for the
      next mission.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10
    m_Localized: Read the text about the destination of proteins after their synthesis
      and processing and answer the quiz to conclude your journey!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11
    m_Localized: 'For the GCC codon, this is the pathway you should look at in the
      table to synthesize its respective amino acid: Ala - (Alanine).'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12
    m_Localized: Ala - (Alanine)
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
